# tools/gates/lean.axioms -- every axiom a Bebop.* declaration may rest on (tools/gates/lean.sh check 2).
# DERIVED, not typed: `sh tools/gates/lean.sh --census | awk '/^AXIOM/{print $2}'` (Lean.collectAxioms,
# what `#print axioms` reports, over every constant in every Bebop.* module). Census 2026-10-09,
# W-LEANCI, Lean 4.33.1: "lean-axioms: 32 axiom(s) over 1981 constant(s) in 14 module(s)";
# Re-derived 2026-10-09, W-FPMUL (fp_mul_correct now a theorem): "lean-axioms: 31 axiom(s) over 2047 constant(s) in 14 module(s)".
# A new line here is a new trusted assumption: say in the commit what it assumes and why it is true.
# A line nothing uses any more is red too -- delete it. `sorryAx` is never allowed.
#
# Lean's three standard axioms.
# 26 syscall specifications (Bebop/Syscalls.lean): what a sys_* builtin does is the OS's, not the model's.
# (fp_mul_correct was listed here until 2026-10-09; W-FPMUL proved it, kernel-only, and deleted the line.)
# Two bv_decide certificates checked by native code (Lean compiler + CaDiCaL in the trust root, not kernel-only).
